+      # ...AND SO DOES THE TAG PATH, which the check above does not cover.
+      # A tag names whatever commit its pusher chooses, and the pushed-tag
+      # guard below only compares the tag NAME with ts/package.json — so a
+      # `v*` tag pushed from an unmerged branch carrying a bumped version
+      # passes every existing check and publishes unreviewed code. npm never
+      # allows republishing a version, so that cannot be taken back.
+      #
+      # Containment is the invariant both entry points actually need, and it
+      # is the same question for each: on a dispatch from main it passes
+      # trivially, on a tag push it does the work. The branch-name check above
+      # stays because it fails earlier and says so more clearly.
+      - name: The released commit must be on main
+        run: |
+          set -euo pipefail
+          git fetch --no-tags --depth=0 origin main
+          if ! git merge-base --is-ancestor "$GITHUB_SHA" origin/main; then
+            echo "::error::$GITHUB_SHA is not contained in origin/main; refusing to release it"
+            exit 1
+          fi
+          echo "$GITHUB_SHA is on main"
+
